{
 "about": "Which clip a shared or pasted text names. The page's parseLink (engine/crate.html) and the share extension's SharedInbox.shareLink (ios/Addify/SharedInbox.swift) read text by the same rule, so a share and a paste of the same text scan the same clip. engine/test_round7c.py checks parseLink against every case here.",
 "rule": [
  "1. Every http(s) link in the text is a candidate, in order; the first candidate that is a clip wins (unchanged).",
  "2. With no http(s) link, the leading run of URL characters (leading characters in strip_leading dropped first, trailing characters in strip_trailing dropped after; the whole text when that run is empty) is the next candidate (unchanged).",
  "3. ROUND 7C: with no http(s) link and no clip from step 2, split the text into words on the separators below. For each word, in order: remove every zero-width character, then drop the leading characters in strip_leading, then drop the trailing characters in strip_trailing, then test the word as a clip (https:// is added when it has no scheme). The first word that is a clip wins.",
  "4. A profile, sound, tag, story or other page link never wins over a clip that comes after it. With no clip anywhere, the result is no clip; the page then names the app of a page link found in step 1 or 2 ('page')."
 ],
 "separators": "Unicode White_Space: U+0009-U+000D, U+0020, U+0085, U+00A0, U+1680, U+2000-U+200A, U+2028, U+2029, U+202F, U+205F, U+3000",
 "zero_width": [
  "U+200B",
  "U+200C",
  "U+200D",
  "U+2060",
  "U+FEFF"
 ],
 "strip_leading": "([{<\"'",
 "strip_trailing": ".,;:!?'\"()[]{}<>*",
 "clip_shapes": "tiktok.com (www., m.): /@user/video/<6-25 digits>, /@user/photo/<6-25 digits>, /t/<5-16 alnum>, /v/<6-25 digits>(.html); vm.tiktok.com or vt.tiktok.com: /<5-16 alnum> or /t/<5-16 alnum>; instagram.com or instagr.am (www., m.): /(<user>/)(reel|reels|p|tv)/<5-40 code>. A trailing slash is allowed. instagr.am is handed on as www.instagram.com.",
 "fields": {
  "clip": "the link parseLink hands on to the scan, exactly, or null when the text names no clip",
  "key": "the video that link names: https:// + host in lower case without www. or m. + path without its trailing slash, no query (the page's stripClip). A port that hands on another spelling of the same link matches on key",
  "page": "with no clip: the app whose page link the page names in its 'not a clip' message (TikTok or Instagram), else null"
 },
